    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d675">

                <pb facs="0818" n="804" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg804"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense(M)/13533: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-06-18T11:15:00-04:30">June 18, 1943—11:15
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 21—3 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–333. For Rosenthal, BEW,<anchor n="38" xml:id="d675-f1"/> from
                        Eisenhardt.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d675-f2"/> Department’s A–645 of June
                        10<anchor n="40" xml:id="d675-f3"/> advising delay of cinchona survey until
                    conclusion <pb facs="0819" n="805" xml:id="pg805"/> of rainy season, we strongly
                    recommend that you reconsider your decision and make arrangements for promptest
                    possible start.</p>
                <p>We have thoroughly checked reliable sources information regarding transportation
                    in prospective cinchona areas and have ascertained that no important delays will
                    be encountered even during heaviest rainy season. Furthermore, we consider that
                    further delays will have detrimental effect on interest already aroused locally
                    for collaboration with our program.</p>
                <p>We anxiously await your further advices on this matter. [Eisenhardt.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
